// This file is the QA-02 VERIFICATION of the health-check finding C-01
// (audit/health_report.md P1): two unchecked type assertions
// `doc["_stages"].([]map[string]any)` — at enrich.go:148 (appendStage) and
// worker.go:291 (attemptedNoWork) — that discard the `ok` value.
//
// Root cause: appendStage builds _stages in memory as []map[string]any, so WITHIN a
// single workItem pass both assertions succeed. But persistRow marshals the whole
// document (including _stages) to JSON, and decodeDoc (worker.go) unmarshals it
// back into map[string]any. encoding/json decodes a JSON array as []any (NOT
// []map[string]any), so the unchecked assertions silently yield nil/false on a
// round-tripped doc: appendStage would OVERWRITE prior history (data loss) and
// attemptedNoWork could not observe a prior-pass stage.
//
// FIX LANDED: decodeDoc now normalizes _stages from []any to []map[string]any at
// the decode boundary (worker.go normalizeStages), so both readers see the
// in-memory form across every store round-trip. The assertions below verify the
// CORRECTED behavior: a round-tripped _stages stays readable ([]map[string]any),
// attemptedNoWork reads a prior-pass unavailable stage, appendStage PRESERVES the
// audit history (len grows, not resets), and a re-derive workItem keeps the
// tv-parser:ok entry. See docs/async-enrichment/qa/debug_brief.md.
